#
# golden.swarm — which swarm disc each model from build_system/golden.models
# goes on, one "<group> <model name>" per line. Each group becomes one swarm
# disc, numbered from 2 in the order groups first appear here:
# dist/discs/zxv-swarm-disc<N>-<group>.img, its partition named
# ZXV_SWARM_<GROUP>. Swarm discs hold no machine code, so the same discs
# serve every architecture's core disc. A disc may not pass 1.8 GB; split a
# group that grows past it. Models in build_system/golden.core go on the
# core disc instead, and every model is on exactly one disc.
#
# Groups: 1-16 characters of a-z and 0-9 (vision, audio, reason, ...).

reason qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
